# Who may sign commits on foundry projects, for git to verify signatures
# (git log --show-signature, git verify-commit). session-init points
# gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile here, so agents can check each other's commits.
# GitHub doesn't read this file: it verifies against each user's uploaded keys.
#
# One line per signer:  <email> <public key>
#   - each role: the user.email and signingkey in roles/<role>/gitconfig,
#     whose key is the public half of secrets/ssh/<role>;
#   - you, so merges and commits of yours on main verify too.
# Roles that share a GitHub user (planner, for now, uses architect's) share
# a line. tests/agent_kit/test_allowed_signers.py keeps this in step with the
# role gitconfigs.
